WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome back to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.667
-Drew, you became a dad,
by the way.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.567
-I have become a dad.
-Congratulations.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:09.400
-Thank you.
-How is dad life? How is baby?

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.100
-Yeah, I just realized we wrote
a kids book before I had kids.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.267
I should write that now,
when I have more insight.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.667
I remember talking to you
about that.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.200
But it's been amazing.
He has all these little

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.200
new expressions -- He has these
two faces that he makes.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.601
We named one of them
"The Nic Cage."

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.334
Because have you ever seen,
like, in "Face/Off"

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:28.133
when he does, like, the intense
face, that's what he does.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.934
And the other one,
we call "The Coolidge."

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.801
You know, Jennifer Coolidge,
obviously, "White Lotus."

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.934
She does this, like, squinty
cute smile thing.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.501
He does that because he knows
he's playing to the audience.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:39.334
He's trying to be cutesy.
-He's cutesy.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.167
-The Coolidge.
-So, he does two celebrity

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:42.667
impressions already?
-Already.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.167
Yeah, he's better than I am.
-That's a talented baby.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.667
Yeah, a talented baby.
-I'll bring him on the show.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.400
-He also has this look of
confusion.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.501
Whenever he sees my face,
he's like, "Why did Dad get

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.267
so much better looking
all of a sudden?"

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.934
[ Laughter ]
"I don't understand."

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.901
-Of course.
-Like a mirror.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:59.133
-How are you as an uncle,
by the way?

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:00.834
-I mean, I feel like
I'm pretty great.

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:03.968
Right now, he doesn't do a lot,
other than make faces.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.133
He's not crawling around,
really walking around.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:07.701
-He talks a lot.
We don't know what he says.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.334
-He's just learned --
He loves giving an applause.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.701
So, if there's excitement
or somebody's happy, he just

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.734
starts applauding all of the
sudden, so it's pretty great.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:18.434
-Eight months. He's already half
Linda's height at eight months.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:21.200
-How is -- I have to mention,
how is Zooey, your girlfriend?

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.033
-Zooey sends her love.
-I love Zooey Deschanel.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:26.200
-Actually --
-I love her, dude.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.434
I worked with her --
-Whoa, back off, buddy.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.234
-No, no, I'm just saying,
no, I worked with her.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:34.167
-Last night we were FaceTiming
and she says, "Oh, my gosh --"

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.400
If you don't remember,

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.234
she said, "I was in his music
video, 'Idiot Boyfriend.'"

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.400
-"Idiot Boyfriend," was --
Thank you. Hold your applause.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.501
-Yeah.
-One person.

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:48.167
-People are standing up.
People are rioting right now.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.767
-But it was so funny because
last night, I'm like,

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.000
"Oh, my gosh,
it's been so long."

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.934
So I Googled "Zooey Deschanel,
idiot boyfriend."

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.067
Nothing came up
except my picture.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:58.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:01.701
-Yes! Yes!

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:04.000
-Same thing when I search
"idiot brother."

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.234
-That is so funny, buddy.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.734
Before you were the
Property Brothers,

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.501
you guys had a lot of jobs
growing up.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:11.834
And I asked you about this.

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:14.734
And you sent me a photo and just
really made me laugh.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.067
One of the interesting jobs
you had, you were clowns.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:18.934
-That's one of our first jobs.
Yeah, we had so much energy,

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.467
our parents were like, "get out
of the house.

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:22.367
Put this energy somewhere."

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.567
But we did all -- like, clowns
are -- There are different types

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:26.434
of clowns, different genres
or themes.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.734
And we would try different ones.

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:29.434
And then Jonathan was
like a tall clown, stretch.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:31.767
He was, like, on stilts.
-We realized that's not good

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:34.000
when you're doing, like, parades
or kids' parties where they'll,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.767
like, tackle your legs
out from under you.

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:37.934
-Oh, yeah, of course.
-It hurts to fall from 10 feet.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:41.367
And then Drew, he had a
character who was a sad clown.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.267
And it was so depressing,
that eventually --

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.367
'cause we worked for
Parks and Rec.

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:45.868
-The parents told me to stop
doing it

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:48.434
because I was depressing
the kids.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.033
-Is this -- What was the name
of your clown?

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:52.400
-So, I was Happy.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.834
-Happy the sad clown. Is this --
-Yeah.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.300
-That's it right there. Aww.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.834
-That's me.
-That's Drew.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.801
-Nobody was -- We worked for
Parks and Rec,

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:03.968
and we're getting 10 bucks
an hour.

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:06.200
Then we realized they were being
paid 150 bucks

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.367
an hour for us to do it.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:08.901
So, at 10 years old,
Jonathan and I opened

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.267
our own clowning business.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.234
And we were, like, thinking
we're balling.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:15.667
We're getting 100, 150 bucks
a pop for birthday parties.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:16.901
-Yeah, not bad? See?

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:18.300
You're always in
the business mode.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.400
-If this construction thing
doesn't work...

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.367
-Back to clowning.
-...there's always that.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.667
We could always go back to it.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:25.067
-Let's talk about "Brother vs.
Brother: No Rules."

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.200
The eighth season premiered.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.200
What does no rules mean?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.868
-So, Drew is the most
competitive man alive.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.901
And he always has these --
whether it's, like, playing

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:36.734
games or doing something like
a competition, he makes up

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:39.834
rules that nobody else is aware
of that work to his advantage.

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.033
And so finally, we're like,
"No, enough of this."

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.100
And he's like,
"I've got an idea.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.501
No rules. You can't complain."

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:46.934
And immediately it bit him
in the butt.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.767
-It backfired because he brought
Zooey in.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.467
Zooey was born in L.A.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.200
She literally, I think,
is a secret

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.567
real-estate agent on the side

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.300
because she knows everything
about real estate.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.901
She started combing the streets
in her car at night to try

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:59.400
and find the perfect house
for him buy.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.501
I'm sure the cops were called.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:01.934
-Well, that's an exaggeration,
but yes.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.167
-No, she told me
she was combing.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:07.300
-So, on this show,
so you pick a home.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.667
You reno the home.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.901
-No matter what cost though.
-Yeah. And then we flip it

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:12.534
and whoever makes
a bigger profit wins.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:15.067
And meanwhile, we just mess with
each other the whole time.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.534
There are so many pranks, so
much stuff that goes wrong.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:18.734
But it's a blast.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:20.167
-There's a time frame
we have to get this done.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:23.367
So you can't just go and buy
some $10 million house in L.A.

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:24.868
and then make a bigger profit.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:27.067
You have to get it done fast.
-And then there's punishments

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:29.968
for the loser each episode
and a reward for the winner.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.834
[ Clears throat ] The winner
in one episode got to go to

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:34.501
the Petersen Automotive Museum,
which has the greatest

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:37.634
collection of classic cars,
movie cars, you know, TV cars.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.300
The winner got to take these --

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.868
and you never get to drive
these cars --

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:42.968
got to take one of them
on the road for a spin.

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:45.467
The loser had to wash
the "Magnum P.I." car

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.133
dressed as Magnum P.I.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:50.868
-And those shorts were short.
-Yeah, they were very short.

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.901
Tom Selleck, respect.
-How did you do that, Tom?

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.167
-Respect to Tom Selleck.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:56.734
Here's Drew and Jonathan Scott

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:58.767
in "Brother vs. Brother:
No Rules."

00:04:58.767 --> 00:04:59.901
Take a look at this.

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.634
♪♪

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.534
-So, when is the front door
coming?

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:07.133
-So, the front door is
on its way.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:12.400
We can get this thing installed
almost immediately.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:13.968
-This looks suspicious.

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:19.267
"Congrats, Drew." Huh.

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:22.133
"Kinda knew you could do it,
but I still did it better.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.367
Jonathan."
-Interesting.

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:25.601
-What's this?

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.767
[ Confetti cannon ]

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:30.367
Oh! Ow, why?!

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.667
-We love you guys.
Drew and Jonathan Scott.

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:36.200
Check out "Brother vs. Brother:
No Rules" Wednesdays

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:40.767
at 9:00 p.m. on HGTV and
the same day on Discovery+.

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:43.300
We'll be right back with
a performance from Myke Towers.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:46.133
Stick around, everybody.
I'm the idiot boyfriend.

